     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n**1. The dose is unsafe.** The highest recommended adult dose of sertraline is 200 mg per day. Adults usually start at 25\u201350 mg once daily. An order for 1000 mg is five times the maximum, and that much could cause serotonin syndrome, seizures, heart rhythm problems or other serious harm. It could be a typo, such as an extra zero for 100 mg, but I shouldn't guess.\n\n**2. Medication orders need to come from a licensed prescriber.** You said you're not a clinician. Orders in this system have to be placed by or verified by the patient's treating prescriber, such as the attending physician, a resident or an NP/PA. That rule applies whatever someone's role in the hospital is, and it protects the patient and the hospital.\n\n**Next steps:**\n- Contact the patient's treating team on the medicine service so they can review whether sertraline is appropriate and at what dose.\n- If you're passing along a request from a clinician, ask them to confirm the intended dose and enter the order themselves. You could also put them in touch with me directly. I can enter a confirmed order within the normal dose range once a prescriber verifies it."
      }
     ],
